$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{5})+(\goldD{13})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{9}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $h(\blueD{9})$:

$\begin{align}
h(\blueD{9})&=-(\blueD{9}-5)(\blueD{9}-13)
\\\\
&=-(4)(-4)
\\\\
&=16
\end{align}$
